cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
title: "fourcover-search: an open-source four-descent and Elkies-type lattice search for rational points on elliptic curves"
authors:
  - family-names: Kudriashov
    given-names: Aleksei
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-8885-5338"
abstract: >-
  A pipeline with no Magma dependency: PARI 2-descent, C. D. Long's relative four-descent, reduction of the four-cover,
  and an Elkies-type lattice search on the intersection of two quadrics in P^3. Following Elkies (2000), the search uses
  higher-order (osculating) boxes along the real locus; geometry and LLL use quad precision, enumeration uses long
  double, and candidates undergo fixed-width integer checks whose exactness requires avoiding overflow.
  Completeness is not certified. The pipeline found generators for y^2 = x^3 + 730033053750 using elkies4 and
  y^2 = x^3 + 428843415 using elkies4q, both listed in the public Best-Matschke S6 unknown data at c31a0f6.
  Their generator proofs include independent arbitrary-precision checks; historical priority remains unresolved.
  Our code is MIT-licensed; our generated data and documentation are CC BY 4.0. Dependencies retain their own licenses. The search code, pipeline and proofs were produced by AI agents (Anthropic Claude;
  OpenAI Codex cores for adversarial audits) under the direction of the author of record, who takes responsibility for
  the content.
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
